      <activity id="69eabe0a-25b3-5555-8555-a86ac8eb9371" activityNameId="f78cafbf-4641-5f4c-b9a3-03d739a42b69" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed  [36dcdcb0d1]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, PEM using electricity from Solar PV + Wind (MA)
This dataset represents the supply of 1 kilowatt hour of electricity in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, PEM, with electricity from Solar PV + Wind (MA) as feedstock. Electricity conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 45%. LHV [kWh/kg]: 33.33. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.88. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 3ad53529-7aea-3aa6-8590-33ebfbcdfd58
Location: 
